0458: a sampling profiler for one process (sweetprof=NAME) and finer display statistics.

S5v 2026-11-15: with the present path fixed (0457) the pointer is smooth, but window drags, scrolling and
animations stay slow. Nothing on the phone could say where a process spends its CPU.

- osfmk/kern/exception.c: boot-arg sweetprof=NAME (e.g. WindowServer). A kernel thread cross-calls the other
  started cores 500 times a second (cpu_xcall, never waiting for a core); in each core's interrupt, if the
  interrupted thread belongs to NAME, the interrupted pc and lr are counted in 16-byte buckets, user and kernel
  apart, with the thread id. bsd/dev/starlte_smp.c's STARLTE TOP loop calls sweet_prof_report() every 10 s:
  "SWEET PROF name[pid]: N samples (...) slide mh kslide", "SWEET PROF t:" (threads with their names),
  "SWEET PROF u:" / "k:" (pc:lr:count, busiest first), and once "SWEET PROF img" (dyld's image list outside the
  shared cache). Only windows with 250 samples or more are printed. tools/macos/prof-report.py names the functions.
- SweetFramebuffer.cpp: "SWEET FB STATS" every 2 s while frames come (was 10 s), with the swaps WindowServer
  handed in (frame / pointer) and the average and longest present time.
Kernel seq2d = seq2c + 0458.

